    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 27; printed page 5, continuation of Section 1.1.2",
      "anchor": "the integral conservation law (1.10) is the more fundamental equation which does continue to hold",
      "observation": "The source asserts continued validity of the integral conservation law at discontinuities where the classical differential equation fails, without specifying a precise derivative or trace interpretation here."
    }
